# apps/cli structure (FSD)

The whole CLI is organised like our React apps: Feature-Sliced Design with four layers under
`apps/cli/src`. Imports only go **down**: `app` → `views` → `features` → `shared`.

```
src/app/        entry and routing: index.ts (bin), main.ts, process-context.ts, commands/<name>-command.ts
src/views/      one folder per area: what a command runs and the terminal screens it shows
src/features/   one folder per domain slice, with segments
src/shared/     cross-cutting code that knows nothing about reviews: ui, hooks, lib
```

## app

The equivalent of routes. Thin.

- `commands/<name>-command.ts` holds one citty `defineCommand`: its name, description and argument schema, and a
  `run` that calls one function from a view. No logic, no printing.
- `main.ts` registers the commands; `process-context.ts` builds the real `CliContext`; `index.ts` is the bin entry.
- Nothing imports from `app`.

## views

A view is a screen or a command runner that composes features and shared code. It owns layout, key handling,
argument handling and printing, and holds no domain rules.

- Terminal screens: `<name>-view.tsx` exporting `<Name>View` (`home-view.tsx` → `HomeView`).
- Command runners: `run-<command>.ts` exporting one function, plus the small files it needs
  (`review-args.ts`, `progress-printer.ts`). One function per file.
- Launchers that mount a screen: `launch-<name>.tsx` (`launch-review.tsx` → `openTui`).
- Areas: `review`, `home`, `run`, `history`, `providers`, `rules`, `apply`, `doctor`, `init`. A view may import
  another view (`run` shows the `review` view); keep that rare.
- A file over ~250 lines is split: keys into `use-<name>-keys.ts`, prompts and overlays into their own files.

## features

A feature is a domain slice: `features/<domain>/`. Segments:

- `ui/` presentational components of the slice.
- `lib/` pure logic, one function per file (`build-stream.ts`, `parse-query.ts`, `markdown-report.ts`).
- `hooks/` hooks that hold the slice's behaviour (`use-switching.tsx`).
- `model/` state and actions of the slice (`session.ts`).
- A feature **never imports another feature**. When two slices must work together a view composes them; a type
  both need moves to `@crit/schema` or `shared`.

Slices today: `review-session`, `review-history`, `review-report`, `provider-setup`, `model-switching`,
`run-progress`.

## shared

Infrastructure and primitives only: nothing that knows about findings, reviews or providers.

- `shared/ui` terminal components, one per file (`panel.tsx`, `picker.tsx`, `footer.tsx`, `render-full-screen.tsx`).
- `shared/hooks` generic hooks (`use-tick.ts`).
- `shared/lib` pure helpers and infrastructure (`cli-context.ts`, `errors.ts`, `colors.ts`, `format.ts`,
  `table.ts`, `text.ts`, `theme.ts`, `highlight.ts`, `prompter.ts`, `clipboard.ts`).
- If two features need the same helper, promote it to `shared` and delete the copies.

## Imports

- **No barrel files** under `apps/cli`: no `index.ts` re-exports. Import from the file that defines the name.
- Imports across folders use the alias: `import { Panel } from "@/shared/ui/panel.tsx"`. `@/` is `apps/cli/src`
  (tsconfig `paths`, mirrored in the vitest config; tsdown reads tsconfig).
- Siblings in the same folder use `./name.ts`. Never `../`.
- Commands load the screens lazily: `await import("@/views/review/launch-review.tsx")`, so Ink is only loaded
  when a screen is shown.
- Tests live in `apps/cli/test`, import with `@/`, and are named after the file under test.

## Adding code: where does it go?

| You are adding                                          | Put it in                                          |
| ------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |
| A new CLI command                                       | `app/commands/<name>-command.ts` + `views/<name>/run-<name>.ts` |
| A box, list, prompt or key bar usable by any screen     | `shared/ui`                                        |
| A pure function that decides what to show or print      | `features/<slice>/lib`                             |
| State a screen reads and the actions it calls           | `features/<slice>/model`                           |
| A new screen or overlay                                 | `views/<area>/<name>-view.tsx`                     |
| A way to start a screen from a command                  | `views/<area>/launch-<name>.tsx`                   |
| Something two slices need                               | `shared`, or a view that composes both slices      |
